            "issues": [
              {
                "kind": "MULTI",
                "cue_idx": 4,
                "start_s": 28.83,
                "n_sentences": 3,
                "text": "System 1 is fast. Automatic. Instinctive."
              },
              {
                "kind": "GAP",
                "cue_idx": 4,
                "start_s": 28.83,
                "next_start_s": 57.93,
                "gap_s": 29.1,
                "text": "System 1 is fast. Automatic. Instinctive."
              },
              {
                "kind": "MULTI",
                "cue_idx": 5,
                "start_s": 57.93,
                "n_sentences": 3,
                "text": "System 2 is slow. Deliberate. Analytical."
              },
              {
                "kind": "GAP",
                "cue_idx": 5,
                "start_s": 57.93,
                "next_start_s": 82.57,
                "gap_s": 24.64,
                "text": "System 2 is slow. Deliberate. Analytical."
              },
              {
                "kind": "MULTI",
                "cue_idx": 7,
                "start_s": 90.15,
                "n_sentences": 2,
                "text": "The fix isn't to think less. It's to train your mind to step back."
              }
            ]
          },
          "ffprobe_duration_s": null,
          "whisper_segments": [
            {
              "start_s": 1.07,
              "end_s": 6.75,
              "text": "Day 2. Yesterday I told you this training is built on science. Today I want to show you"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 6.75,
              "end_s": 11.15,
              "text": "the exact science because once you understand what's actually happening in your brain"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 11.15,
              "end_s": 17.91,
              "text": "when you choke, you can't unsee it. So in 2002 a psychologist named Daniel Keniman won"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 17.91,
              "end_s": 23.19,
              "text": "the Nobel Prize and his research explains something that changes how you think about"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 23.19,
              "end_s": 30.11,
              "text": "every high pressure moment you've ever had. He found that the brain runs on two systems."
            },
            {
              "start_s": 30.11,
              "end_s": 36.39,
              "text": "System 1 is fast, automatic, instinctive. When you've done something thousands of times"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 36.39,
              "end_s": 42.59,
              "text": "of free throw, a distance you've run a thousand times, a survey hit since you were 12. System"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 42.59,
              "end_s": 50.63,
              "text": "1 handles it. It doesn't think. It just executes. And that's what flow state is. That's what"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 50.63,
              "end_s": 56.27,
              "text": "people mean when they say something is in the zone or someone is in the zone. System 1"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 56.27,
              "end_s": 64.39,
              "text": "is running the show. System 2 is slow, deliberate, analytical. System 2 is what kicks in when"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 64.39,
              "end_s": 70.43,
              "text": "you're overthinking. When you're thinking about your form on a rep you've done 10,000"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 70.43,
              "end_s": 75.67,
              "text": "times. When you're thinking about the split you just ran. When you're thinking about"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 75.67,
              "end_s": 80.99,
              "text": "who's next to you, what your coach is going to say, whether you have enough left. But"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 80.99,
              "end_s": 87.59,
              "text": "here's the glitch. Choking is what happens when System 2 tries to take control of something"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 87.59,
              "end_s": 95.91,
              "text": "System 1 already owns. The fix isn't to think less. It's to train your mind to step back"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 95.91,
              "end_s": 103.47,
              "text": "and let System 1 do its job. That's what every drill in this app is doing. Right now I want"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 103.47,
              "end_s": 109.51,
              "text": "you to find your version of that moment. On your screen you're going to log it and"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 109.51,
              "end_s": 114.15,
              "text": "that identify exactly what your brain was doing instead of competing."
            }
          ],
          "whisper_segment_count": 18
        },
