            {
              "start_s": 8.4,
              "end_s": 13.78,
              "text": "under pressure, but today we build the tool that ties all of it together. It's called"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 13.78,
              "end_s": 22.98,
              "text": "a focus anchor. Every elite performer has one. A word, a short phrase, or a physical sensation"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 22.98,
              "end_s": 30.14,
              "text": "that their mind comes back to when it starts to drift. Some of them chose it deliberately."
            },
            {
              "start_s": 30.14,
              "end_s": 37.94,
              "text": "Just stumbled onto it. Today, you choose yours on purpose. Here's what makes a good anchor."
            },
            {
              "start_s": 37.94,
              "end_s": 45.5,
              "text": "It should be short, one or two words max. It should be process focused, not outcome focused."
            },
            {
              "start_s": 45.5,
              "end_s": 52.34,
              "text": "It puts you in your body and in the moment, not in your head. Some examples are like next"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 52.34,
              "end_s": 60.78,
              "text": "play, breathe, process, here, trust, but it has to be yours. Before we start, take one box"
            },
            {
              "start_s": 60.78,
              "end_s": 69.98,
              "text": "breath to settle it. And for four, hold for four, out for four, hold for four. Then we find your anchor."
            }
          ],
